{0 Proffer}

This library provides declarative HTTP serving. A handler describes a response
and calls the responder it is given. A backend consumes the description and
owns the wire. Dispatch, conditional requests and HEAD are consequently
decided once and behave the same in the mock and socket backends.

Route constructors take their handler at [portable], so state and codecs a
handler needs reach it through the per-domain ['env] argument.

{1 Entry points}

- {!module:Proffer} contains requests, responses, typed routing, sites and the
  shared dispatcher.
- {!module:Proffer_mock} runs a site against synthetic requests with no
  sockets.
- [Proffer_httpz], in the [proffer-httpz] package, serves a site over HTTP/1.1
  with httpz and Eio.

{1 Quick start}

{[
  open Proffer
  open Proffer.Route

  let site =
    Site.of_routes
      [ get root (fun () _req respond -> Resp.text respond "index")
      ; get (s "hello" / str) (fun who () _req respond ->
          Resp.text respond ("hello " ^ who))
      ]

  let () =
    Eio_main.run @@ fun stdenv ->
    Proffer_httpz.run stdenv ~env:() site
]}

{1 Forms}

A body posted by an HTML form arrives in one of two encodings.
[application/x-www-form-urlencoded] is read by {!Proffer.Req.form_result},
which reports a body of another media type rather than passing it off as an
empty form, by {!Proffer.Req.form} where that distinction does not matter, and
by {!Proffer.Req.form_param} for a single field. The same encoding as a codec
is {!Proffer.Media.form}, which {!Proffer.Route.with_body} accepts like any
other.

[multipart/form-data], the encoding of a form carrying a file, is read by
{!Proffer.Multipart.of_req}. Its parts are named by
{!Proffer.Multipart.field}, {!Proffer.Multipart.file} and
{!Proffer.Multipart.fields}. A body is held whole in memory, so the backend's
request cap is the upload limit.

{1 Backend authors}

{!module:Proffer.Backend} applies routing, conditional requests, and HEAD to a
parsed request and produces an outcome. Applications using a shipped backend
do not need to call it directly.
